From fbacb56f0d5a38c6841beb0a2d98d7470bb250ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): a Desktop terminal batch timeout stops the batch,
 not the turn [daveey]

Problem: in a Desktop session, a message with 2+ terminal calls is prepared as a
batch. When one command passed the sequential deadline, the turn ended with no
reply (self-heal plugin-9605e451d0: 10-27 11:17 PT, row 593750 "timed out after
420.0s", then a hidden "[interrupt: no assistant output for this turn]"; David
asked "why did you stop" 55 min later).

Why: the prepared-call timeout branch in _run_sequential_tool_execution_middleware
called agent.interrupt(tool_reason="terminal batch timeout") after
prepared.batch.close(). close() already keeps later prepared commands from
starting; the interrupt only added a turn abort, so the model never saw the
timeout. Batch preparation timeouts had the same abort.
Not caught: tests pinned the "terminal_batch_timeout" issuer label; none checked
that the model still gets a turn after a tool timeout on the batch path.

Fix: _TerminalBatch.stop(notice) records a stop notice and closes the batch. A
command timeout and a preparation timeout call it instead of interrupting. The
sequential loop reports every unstarted call with "[Not run: ... timed out]"
and the turn goes on to the next model call, as it does outside a batch. User
stops keep their attribution, message and redirect.

Proof: tests/agent/test_terminal_batch_timeout_continues.py runs a real Desktop
run_conversation with 3 terminal calls (2nd over a 3 s deadline): on main
final_response=None, Turn ended reason=interrupted_by_system(terminal_batch_timeout);
with the fix REPORTED, 2 model calls, the 3rd command never runs. Also covers the
preparation timeout and stop() closing at once. Mutants: dropping the loop check,
the prep stop, or stop()'s close each fail a test. 17 files / 370 tests pass.
